Subject: HWUI: let go of an idle window's surface and the buffers its queue holds

A window's buffer queue holds the buffer on screen and the free ones the app draws its next
frames into (three more for the Settings app, 7 MiB each at 1208x1383), and keeps them while the
window draws nothing. Each is a GPU buffer on the host. Discarding the queue's free buffers alone
would not free them: the window's surface (ANGLE's Vulkan swapchain under the EGL surface, or
HWUI's own VulkanSurface) imported every buffer it dequeued and keeps the import, and the app's
references keep SurfaceFlinger's cached copy too.

At the idle release 0014 adds, after 30 seconds without a frame, each window now lets go of its
GPU surface (IRenderPipeline::releaseSurfaceWhileIdle) and keeps its native window, the state a
trim that destroys the GPU context leaves (onContextDestroyed). Destroying the surface
disconnects the window's queue, which frees every buffer in it but the one SurfaceFlinger shows,
so the window keeps its last picture on screen. The app's buffers then die, which uncaches them
in SurfaceFlinger, and the surface's depth and stencil image goes too. The idle release's
waited-on submit makes ANGLE free what it deferred. The log line of 0014 counts the windows:

  No frame for N s: let go of the surfaces of W windows and K KiB of GPU caches (R resources);
  L KiB remain

The next frame makes the surface again in makeCurrent(), as after a trim, and draws the whole
window (it has a new surface). A frame the render thread draws on its own (an animation, a
RenderNode drawn directly) makes it again first too. makeCurrent() also sets again what
setupPipelineSurface() set on the window (frame timestamps, freeze scaling), which the
disconnect forgot. That first frame dequeues and so allocates new buffers. A window that draws
into a hardware buffer, or has no surface, is left alone.

Applies to frameworks/base at 45034f0663f960d9ee5fb0a101a4732b71f6e2f4 (Android 16), after 0014.
---
diff --git a/libs/hwui/pipeline/skia/SkiaOpenGLPipeline.cpp b/libs/hwui/pipeline/skia/SkiaOpenGLPipeline.cpp
index 857f124f..9ff4de76 100644
--- a/libs/hwui/pipeline/skia/SkiaOpenGLPipeline.cpp
+++ b/libs/hwui/pipeline/skia/SkiaOpenGLPipeline.cpp
@@ -229,6 +229,17 @@ void SkiaOpenGLPipeline::onContextDestroyed() {
     }
 }
 
+bool SkiaOpenGLPipeline::releaseSurfaceWhileIdle() {
+    if (mHardwareBuffer || !mNativeWindow || mEglSurface == EGL_NO_SURFACE) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    // Destroying the EGL surface disconnects the window's buffer queue, which frees every buffer
+    // in it but the one on screen. makeCurrent() makes the surface again for the next frame.
+    mEglManager.destroySurface(mEglSurface);
+    mEglSurface = EGL_NO_SURFACE;
+    return true;
+}
+
 void SkiaOpenGLPipeline::onStop() {
     if (mEglManager.isCurrent(mEglSurface)) {
         mEglManager.makeCurrent(EGL_NO_SURFACE);
diff --git a/libs/hwui/pipeline/skia/SkiaVulkanPipeline.cpp b/libs/hwui/pipeline/skia/SkiaVulkanPipeline.cpp
